   "text": [
    {
     "id": "editorial",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "dossier-jung-pauli-psychoid · ARGUED",
     "title": "Jung–Pauli — Psychoid, Number and a Translation That Changes Its Terms",
     "italic": "Paraphrased correspondence and later scholarship; Argued authorial return",
     "body": "",
     "x": 0.033,
     "y": 0.05,
     "width": 470,
     "size": 25,
     "align": "left"
    },
    {
     "id": "body",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "",
     "title": "",
     "italic": "",
     "body": "The Jung–Pauli source house sources a correspondence running from 1932 to 1958. This dossier develops its changing question: how can psychic experience, physical description and mathematical form bear a relation without one vocabulary silently taking possession of the others? Dreams, letters, diagrams and later edited essays are different kinds of witness.",
