     "id": "body",
     "visible": true,
     "kicker": "",
     "title": "",
     "italic": "",
     "body": "Zero's reception concerns what a receiving practice permits a sign to do. A familiar shape can enter a new script, table, calculation or account without carrying all its previous uses into the new setting. Conversely, a new notation can preserve an operation across a change in language and material.",
